<Plain title="About Secure Mac App" description="Who writes Secure Mac App, how we test Mac privacy guides and apps, and how we disclose our own app and affiliate links." path="/about/" h1="About" updated="27 Oct 2026">
  <p>Secure Mac App is a privacy and security resource for Mac users: step-by-step guides, honest app comparisons and a few free tools. We also make <a href="/vault/">Secure Vault for Mac</a>, an encrypted vault app that is currently in private beta.</p>

  <h2>Who writes this</h2>
  <p>Sumeet writes and maintains the site. {/* TODO(owner): add real credentials / background here — E-E-A-T. Do not publish invented ones. */}</p>

  <h2 id="how-we-test">How we test</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Guides.</strong> Every step is run on a current version of macOS, and the page names that version. We note what each method does not protect.</li>
    <li><strong>App comparisons.</strong> Every app is judged on the same criteria: encryption, where the key lives, everyday convenience, platforms, price and whether the code is open.</li>
    <li><strong>Dates.</strong> Pages show when they were last updated. Comparison tables show when prices and features were last checked.</li>
    <li><strong>Corrections.</strong> If we got something wrong, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> and we will fix it and say so.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Disclosures</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Our own app.</strong> When Secure Vault for Mac appears in a comparison, it is labelled "ours", and its limitations are listed like the others.</li>
    <li><strong>Affiliate links.</strong> We don't currently use any. If we ever do, those links are marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code> and noted on the page.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple.</strong> This site is unofficial and not affiliated with Apple Inc. "Mac" and "macOS" are used descriptively only.</li>
  </ul>
</Plain>
